WEBVTT

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:06.410
Losing a bag should not mean losing the way to get it back. This is SeekerTag on a real Solana Seeker.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.863
I continue with Seeker, select my wallet, and approve Sign In With Solana in Seed Vault.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.816
My wallet is my identity. Here are my items.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.509
I add Travel Backpack and keep Backpack as its category.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.285
A private note describes the bag, so I can recognize it.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.864
The public message explains how to arrange a return, without exposing my phone number.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.240
I add one SKR in test tokens.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.643
And reserve it for seven days.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.037
Before signing, I review the devnet network, depositing wallet, network fee, and account creation cost.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.665
I approve the deposit in Seed Vault. After network confirmation, the reward is reserved on chain.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.954
Here is the unique QR code for this backpack.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:04.495
I download and open its PDF: six printable formats, with actual sizes and a scale check.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.163
The same link can be written to an NFC tag. This screen is ready for a physical tag.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.944
If my bag goes missing, I mark the item as lost.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:25.813
On a separate Android session, Alex opens that same tag. The reserved reward is visible.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.812
No account is required. Alex enters a name and a message, then notifies the owner.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.575
The notification arrives on my Seeker and opens our conversation.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.895
I reply from the Seeker, and Alex receives my message in the second session.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.715
We arrange the return inside the app, keeping personal contact details private.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:01.535
To receive the reward, Alex opens Set receiving wallet directly from the conversation.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.233
Alex enters a Solana address. Connecting a wallet is optional.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.496
After reviewing the address, Alex confirms it.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.968
Back on the Seeker, I choose Finish return directly in our conversation.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.592
I review the payout: the finder gets zero point nine five SKR, after the five percent service fee.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.395
After confirming the simulated handover, I sign the payout with the owner wallet.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:37.818
The transaction is confirmed on Solana devnet. The reward is released, and both conversations show the completed return.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.864
One tag, private coordination, and a verifiable reward. That is SeekerTag.
